  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Front Porch",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;\r\n\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; cellpadding=&quot;0&quot; hspace=&quot;0&quot; vspace=&quot;0&quot; align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;\r\n &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;\r\n  &lt;td valign=&quot;top&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding-top:0cm;padding-right:9.0pt;\r\n  padding-bottom:0cm;padding-left:9.0pt&quot;&gt;\r\n  &lt;p style=&quot;margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; The proposed front porch, given its design, scale and\r\n  fenestration details, would detract from the Arts and Crafts character of the\r\n  host property and that of properties within the South Hill Conservation Area.\r\n  The proposal would therefore result in an unduly obtrusive and incongruous\r\n  addition to the original dwellinghouse, failing&amp;nbsp;to respect the character\r\n  and proportions of the dwellinghouse and the visual amenities of the\r\n  conservation area. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the high-quality\r\n  design aspiration of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies\r\n  D1, D3, D4 of The London Plan (2021), Policy GR1, SP2 and HE1 of the Harrow’s Local Plan\r\n  (2021-2041), South Hill Conservation Area Study (2008) and the relevant\r\n  provisions of the adopted Harrow Supplementary Planning Document Residential\r\n  Design Guide (2010).&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n  &lt;/td&gt;\r\n &lt;/tr&gt;\r\n&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;\r\n\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Insufficient\r\ndetails have been provided with regards to the materials/detailing of the\r\nproposed porch. As such, the impacts of the proposal on the character and\r\nappearance of the host property and the integrity of the South Hill\r\nConservation Area cannot be fully understood nor determined. The proposal would\r\ntherefore be contrary to the high-quality design aspiration of the National\r\nPlanning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D1, D3, D4 of The London Plan\r\n(2021), Policy GR1, SP2 and HE1 of the Harrow’s Local Plan (2021-2041), South Hill\r\nConservation Area Study (2008) and the relevant provisions of the adopted\r\nHarrow Supplementary Planning Document Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
